Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:22:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] PhoneWindowManager: ENDCALL wakes the device when it is
 asleep

On a keypad phone without a power button the red ENDCALL key is the only
system key: it hangs up, goes home and then to sleep
(END_BUTTON_BEHAVIOR), and has to wake the screen too. Up to N the key
layout gave it the WAKE flag; since O KeyLayoutMap knows only VIRTUAL,
FUNCTION and GESTURE and rejects a file that uses WAKE, and ENDCALL is not
a KeyEvent wake key, so with the screen off nothing woke the phone.

A down press while not interactive is now a wake key. The hangup and the
long-press power menu are unchanged; the down that wakes marks the key
handled, so its up neither goes home nor puts the device back to sleep.
---
 .../java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java
index ef8fb37aa..e35a5f3d5 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java
@@ -6909,6 +6909,13 @@ public class PhoneWindowManager implements WindowManagerPolicy {
                     } else {
                         mEndCallKeyHandled = true;
                     }
+                    // On a keypad phone the red key is the only system key, so
+                    // it has to wake the screen as well. Up to N the key layout
+                    // said so with the WAKE flag; O and later reject that flag
+                    // (KeyLayoutMap knows VIRTUAL/FUNCTION/GESTURE only).
+                    if (!interactive) {
+                        isWakeKey = true;
+                    }
                 } else {
                     if (!mEndCallKeyHandled) {
                         mHandler.removeCallbacks(mEndCallLongPress);
